    "title": "Gwen Stefani and Gavin Rossdale's 19-year-old son looks like his dad's twin - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jolie Zenna ,\n13 hours ago\nGwen Stefani and Gavin Rossdale’s son Kingston doesn’t just look like his dad’s twin — he’s also following in his rocker footsteps.\nThe 19-year-old has been showing off his musical talents via Instagram lately, and fans in the comments can’t get over the teen’s resemblance to the Bush frontman.\n“You look so much like Gavin❤️” one user commented on a video of the teen playing an original song earlier this month.\nGwen Stefani and Gavin Rossdale’s son Kingston (pictured above) looks like his dad’s twin in new Instagram videos. kingsrossdale_/instagram The 19-year-old has been showing off his musical talents, following in his famous parents’ footsteps. kingsrossdale_/instagram Daily Front Row Fashion Los Angeles Awards 2026 red carpet: Hilary Duff, Tiffany Haddish, Doechii and more\n“Holy crap you look just like your dad,” another added.\nOthers pointed out that Kingston is taking after both of his famous parents with his musicality.\n“Badass just like your family!🔥,” one fan gushed. “Music is in the blood!🔥❤️,” another wrote.\nStefani, 56, and Rossdale, 60, were married for nearly 13 years when rumors swirled that he had cheated with their nanny .\n“You look so much like Gavin❤️” one user commented on a video of the teen, referring to the Bush frontman (pictured here in 2020). Getty Images “Holy crap you look just like your dad,” another added. Getty Images Gavin Rossdale compares co-parenting with Gwen Stefani to a ‘two-lane highway’ that never merges\nThe “Sweet Escape” songstress filed for divorce from her husband in 2015, and it was finalized the following year. They welcomed Kingtson, Zuma, 17, and Apollo, 11, during their marriage.\nSince the exes’ “terrible” split , co-parenting their three sons has been a struggle which they have both been open about.\nLast month, Rossdale compared co-parenting with Stefani to a “two-lane highway” that never merges.\nStefani and Rossdale (seen above in 2011) were married for nearly 13 years before their 2015 divorce. Getty Images Since their split, the exes have struggled to co-parent their three sons, Kingston, Zuma (pictured in 2013) and Apollo. Getty Images CLICK HERE TO SUBSCRIBE TO PAGE SIX DAILY FOR MORE CELEBRITY NEWS\n“It’s a very, it is an interesting kind of… it’s a two-lane highway, you know, but they don’t ever seem to merge, which is fine,” Rossdale said.\nThe English musician further explained that it’s each of them doing the best they can to raise their children.\n“Probably doing the best she can, and I’m doing the best I can. And the kids are growing up, so I’m a proud proponent of the system. It’s fine,” he said.\nThe fashion designer moved on with Blake Shelton (seen above in 2024), whom she says gave her a “second chance at life” after her divorce. gwenstefani/Instagram The country music artist became the stepfather to her three boys when they wed in 2021. blakeshelton/Instagram The fashion designer moved on with Blake Shelton , whom she says gave her a “second chance at life” following her “catastrophe” of a divorce from Rossdale.\n“Something that I wanted since I was a little girl is to be married and have this love that I saw my parents have and have babies,” she told People in 2024.\n“That dream was completely ruined; it was crushed, and I had to figure out how I was going to move forward and make a new dream, and God putting Blake in my life was just that miracle.”\nFor more celebrity and entertainment news, visit pagesix.com.\n11",
